  "question": {
    "text": "The amplitude and phase of a wave that is formed by the superposition of two harmonic travelling waves, $\\mathrm{y}_1(\\mathrm{x}, \\mathrm{t})=4 \\sin (\\mathrm{kx}-\\omega \\mathrm{t})$ and $\\mathrm{y}_2(\\mathrm{x}, \\mathrm{t})=2 \\sin \\left(\\mathrm{kx}-\\omega \\mathrm{t}+\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}\\right)$, are $:$<br/>(Take the angular frequency of initial waves same as $\\omega$)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "xCtRr",
      "text": "$\\left[6, \\frac{2 \\pi}{3}\\right]$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZdRwY",
      "text": "$\\left[6, \\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right]$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "febqg",
      "text": "$\\left[\\sqrt{3}, \\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right]$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "wO95f",
      "text": "$\\left[2 \\sqrt{3}, \\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right]$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/_UboJ-EoPz_OlurzVPsyGm92Pyb5a9x5CjeGdmWSsX0.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/>$\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{array}{l}\\mathrm{A}=\\sqrt{2^2+4^2+2 \\times 2 \\times 4 \\times \\cos 120^{\\circ}} \\\\ \\quad=\\sqrt{12}=2 \\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\tan \\phi=\\frac{2 \\sin 120^{\\circ}}{4+2 \\cos 120^{\\circ}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\phi=\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\end{array}\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
